data_pyrite
# Minimal hand-authored pyrite FeS2 structure for special-position constraint tests.
# Pa-3 (#205): Fe on 4a (0,0,0) [fixed], S on 8c (x,x,x) [coupled: one free parameter, y=z=x].
# Cell/coordinate from published pyrite (a = 5.4179 A, x_S ~= 0.3848). ADPs are illustrative
# but respect the cubic site symmetry (U11=U22=U33, U12=U13=U23) so they exercise the coupled
# ADP constraints. Symops are derived from the H-M symbol by gemmi (24 operations); no explicit
# _symmetry_equiv_pos loop is needed.
_cell_length_a 5.41790
_cell_length_b 5.41790
_cell_length_c 5.41790
_cell_angle_alpha 90.00000
_cell_angle_beta 90.00000
_cell_angle_gamma 90.00000
_cell_volume 159.03350
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P a -3'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 205

